<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- The road types of the Shahid Bahonar Port world, layered over SUMO's own OSM type map.

     SUMO's map opens highway=service to delivery vans, pedestrians and bicycles and to nothing else.
     The airfield perimeter where the guard towers stand, the apron and the drydock approach are all
     mapped as service roads, so under SUMO's map neither the naval traffic (vehicle class army) nor
     the port's cleared traffic (authority) can drive any of them: the sizing scenario's guard rota is refused on every
     one of its 335 postings. This admits both classes on the type and states nothing else, so the
     type's lanes, speed and priority stay SUMO's.

     Read by the world build, which passes SUMO's map first and this second
     (carlacontrol.NetconvertTypeMap), so the network in the world package carries the permission
     and every scenario compiled against the world inherits it.

     What a type map cannot say: which roads are private. OSM marks the port's interior
     access=private, and netconvert reads the access key only as access=no, so a private service road
     and a public one take the same type and the same permissions here. -->
<types>
    <type id="highway.service" allow="delivery pedestrian bicycle army authority"/>
</types>
